Heat the #pan{} with @oil{1%tbsp} and fry @garlic{1%clove}(crushed) for ~{1%minutes}, then stir in @chipotle paste{1%tbsp}.

Tip in @chopped tomatoes{1%tin}, stir and bring to a simmer. Season with @salt{} and simmer until thick. Add @black beans{400%g}(drained) and cook briefly, ensuring any water gets cooked off, then stir in @coriander{}(chopped).

If you are using cold cooked @rice{250%g}(wholegrain) then warm it through, stir in the juice of @lime{}(juiced), @red onion{0.5}(very finely chopped) and @hazelnuts{50%g}(roughly chopped) and season well.

Lay out the @tortilla wraps{4}(large) and sprinkle over some @spinach leaves{}(shredded), add some @?avocado{1}(thinly sliced) and some rice, then top with the bean mix. Add a shake of @hot sauce{} if you like.

Roll the bottom up, then fold the sides in to stop the filling falling out as you roll. Wrap tightly in foil if you like, and cut in half.
